---
import BaseLayout from "../layouts/BaseLayout.astro";
const base = import.meta.env.BASE_URL.endsWith("/") ? import.meta.env.BASE_URL : import.meta.env.BASE_URL + "/";
const product = "https://lordkeremello45.github.io/HWcontrol2.0/";
const source = "https://github.com/lordkeremello45/HWcontrol2.0";
const releases = source + "/releases";
---
<BaseLayout title="HWcontrol Team — Secure, Local-First Hardware Software" description="Discover HWcontrol2.0, an open-source desktop platform for hardware monitoring and capability-gated control. Find beta downloads, platform guidance, security notes and contribution paths.">
  <section class="hero">
    <div>
      <span class="eyebrow">Independent open-source engineering</span>
      <h1>Hardware software, built for real machines.</h1>
      <p class="lead">HWcontrol2.0 is a cross-platform desktop application for hardware telemetry, diagnostics and supported device control. Its design prioritizes local data, explicit hardware capabilities and fail-safe behavior.</p>
      <div class="actions">
        <a class="button primary" href={product}>Explore HWcontrol2.0 <span aria-hidden="true">↗</span></a>
        <a class="button" href={releases}>Browse beta releases</a>
        <a class="button" href={source}>Inspect source code</a>
      </div>
      <p class="fine-print">Beta software. Hardware support depends on the operating system, drivers and detected device capabilities.</p>
    </div>
    <aside class="card hero-panel">
      <span class="pill">How it is structured</span>
      <h2>Separate layers. Clear trust boundaries.</h2>
      <div class="architecture">
        <div><strong>Flutter / Dart</strong><span>Desktop dashboard</span></div>
        <div><strong>Go Bridge</strong><span>Authenticated local IPC</span></div>
        <div><strong>C++ / CMake</strong><span>Native hardware engine</span></div>
        <div><strong>Platform APIs</strong><span>Capability-dependent access</span></div>
      </div>
    </aside>
  </section>

  <section class="section">
    <div class="section-heading">
      <span class="eyebrow">Designed around user control</span>
      <h2>Useful first. Transparent by design.</h2>
    </div>
    <div class="grid">
      <article class="card"><span class="feature-icon" aria-hidden="true">◉</span><h3>Local-first telemetry</h3><p>Hardware readings and routine diagnostic data are intended to remain on the device unless the user explicitly exports or shares them.</p></article>
      <article class="card"><span class="feature-icon" aria-hidden="true">⌁</span><h3>Capability-gated control</h3><p>Control options must reflect the active backend and device support. Unsupported paths should remain unavailable rather than pretending to work.</p></article>
      <article class="card"><span class="feature-icon" aria-hidden="true">✓</span><h3>Inspectable engineering</h3><p>Review the source, release notes, security policy and known limitations before installing a beta build.</p></article>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="split-section section">
    <div>
      <span class="eyebrow">Start here</span>
      <h2>Get from discovery to a useful test.</h2>
      <p class="muted">Choose the platform guide, check the current release assets and follow the verification steps. If a package or hardware path is unavailable, report it with the device and OS details instead of assuming it is supported.</p>
      <div class="actions">
        <a class="button primary" href={`${base}product/`}>Product overview</a>
        <a class="button" href={`${base}getting-started/`}>Getting started</a>
      </div>
    </div>
    <div class="card">
      <h3>Help make the beta better</h3>
      <p>Independent testers are valuable when they report reproducible results across different hardware and operating systems.</p>
      <ul class="compact-list">
        <li>Include OS, architecture and app version.</li>
        <li>Describe expected and actual behavior.</li>
        <li>Remove secrets and personal data from logs.</li>
      </ul>
      <a class="text-link" href={`${base}contribute/`}>Testing and contribution guide →</a>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="section trust-strip">
    <div><strong>Open source</strong><span>Public implementation and issue tracking</span></div>
    <div><strong>No ad tracking</strong><span>No intentional behavioral advertising analytics</span></div>
    <div><strong>Honest beta status</strong><span>Limitations are part of the product information</span></div>
  </section>
</BaseLayout>
